/srv/claude/research/motor-unit-representation/logs/B01-step3-reviewBA-attempt1.log:1069:## 4. Candidate Necessity Claims (Appendix B)
/srv/claude/research/motor-unit-representation/logs/B01-step3-reviewBA-attempt1.log:1265:+Review scope: only the supplied charter, B01 brief, and Proposal A. No other review or draft was consulted. Appendix B itself is absent from these three documents; formal compliance with its actual text cannot be certified. Section 3 evaluates the claim structure and requirements attributed to Appendix B by A.
/srv/claude/research/motor-unit-representation/logs/B01-step3-reviewBA-attempt1.log:1308:+## 3. Audit of Rejected Alternative & Necessity Claim
/srv/claude/research/motor-unit-representation/logs/B01-step3-reviewBA-attempt1.log:1312:+**C-B01-A-01 [CRITICAL].** A supplies explicit premises, scope, conclusion, operational test, and falsifier, and labels the claim Candidate. Its Grade-1 necessity conclusion nevertheless fails for the reasons in §2. Architecture independence also requires realizability and differentiability; derivatives are not directly defined for arbitrary tabular critics.
/srv/claude/research/motor-unit-representation/logs/B01-step3-reviewBA-attempt1.log:1314:+**Falsifiability [MAJOR].** Held-out \(R^2\ge0.99\) is approximate predictive accuracy, not certification of exact measurability or conditional action-support interior. On singleton support, an accurate non-zero derivative is expressly allowed by non-identification, so the proposed falsifier does not refute that branch. The “within 5% of minimum” criterion lacks an independently estimable minimum. Split zeroing and non-identification into separate claims, verify their premises with analytic synthetic controls, and allow premise-satisfying counterexamples to reject the conclusion rather than automatically reclassifying them as premise failures. Appendix B compliance remains unverified without Appendix B's text.
